From b608d0e7a1c587c7aae9e5287de65bcd7489f869 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andy Green <andy@warmcat.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 04:51:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] client: h1: a request is not queued on a connection that said
 connection: close

An h1 client that did not ask to pipeline sends "connection: close", and
the server closes the connection once it has answered.  The client still
keeps that connection warm (LRS_IDLING) on the vhost's active
connections, to absorb the close, and lws_vhost_active_conns() would
queue a later pipelining request to the same place on it.  Unless the
client had already heard the server's close, that request was handed the
connection the server was closing.  The server never read it, and it
failed with "server closed before responding".

An h1 connection whose own request said connection: close is now passed
over when choosing one to queue on.  Another connection to the same
place may still be used.

Backport of upstream 9baa7fb0ae520c0ccca34761559140b823b5f46f (main), adapted to v5.0-stable ac23cae70.
Upstream's lib/sansio/vhost.c is lib/core-net/vhost.c here; the
api-test-http-transfer hunks are dropped.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 lib/core-net/vhost.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/lib/core-net/vhost.c b/lib/core-net/vhost.c
index f61bbda18..48edc32cb 100644
--- a/lib/core-net/vhost.c
+++ b/lib/core-net/vhost.c
@@ -2123,6 +2123,19 @@ lws_vhost_active_conns(struct lws *wsi, struct lws **nwsi, const char *adsin)
 				goto solo;
 			}
 
+			/*
+			 * ...or its own request said "connection: close" (it
+			 * did not ask to pipeline): the server closes it after
+			 * that transaction.  Queued on it, we would be sent on
+			 * a connection already closing, before its kept-warm
+			 * wait has heard the close.  Another to the same place
+			 * may still do.
+			 */
+			if (lwsi_role_h1(w) && !w->client_pipeline) {
+				lwsl_wsi_info(w, "said connection: close");
+				continue;
+			}
+
 #if defined(LWS_WITH_HTTP2)
 			/*
 			 * h2: if in usable state already: just use it without
